From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000035 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tas0dev <156896971+tas0dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mboot: do not reprobe the display synchronously

The PCI publication path already asks the driver core to attach the device.
Calling device_attach() again while late init is still running can enter a GPU
probe path which waits for initialization that cannot progress on this vCPU.
Use the match and bind state left by the first probe instead.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c | 11 ++---------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
index 7c0974100000..333333333333 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
@@ -1033,17 +1033,10 @@ static int __init mboot_wait_for_display_backend(void)
 					       device->info.requester >> 8,
 					       device->info.requester & 0xff);
 		if (pdev) {
-			int attach_result = 1;
-
 			driver_matched = pdev->dev.can_match;
 			driver_bound = device_is_bound(&pdev->dev);
-			if (!driver_bound) {
-				attach_result = device_attach(&pdev->dev);
-				driver_matched = pdev->dev.can_match;
-				driver_bound = device_is_bound(&pdev->dev);
-			}
-			pr_info("mDriver: display probe result %d, matched=%u, bound=%u\n",
-				attach_result, driver_matched, driver_bound);
+			pr_info("mDriver: display matched=%u, bound=%u\n",
+				driver_matched, driver_bound);
 			pci_dev_put(pdev);
 		}
 		if (driver_bound)
